### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example that shows how to create a card that rotates around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the dimensions, colors, or rotation angle to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover state – rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: add a back face for a flip effect */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before { /* Front side */
  background: #fff;
}

.card::after { /* Back side */
  background: #f0f0f0;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front content -->
    <div style="padding: 20px;">
      <h2>Front Side</h2>
      <p>Hover over this card to see the rotation.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` sets a perspective so that 3D transforms look realistic.
2. **Transform-style** – `preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space.
3. **Transition** – `transform 0.6s ease` animates the rotation smoothly.
4. **Hover** – On hover, the card rotates 180 degrees around the Y‑axis.
5. **Backface visibility** – Hides the backside when not visible, preventing flicker.

You can replace the placeholder text with images, icons, or any other content you wish. Adjust the `rotateY(180deg)` value if you want a different rotation angle. Enjoy!
